WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.362
Learn says traffic and remote
network health logs stay thirty days,

2
00:00:04.362 --> 00:00:08.982
names the four tables, and says a sudden
drop in traffic volume is an alert,

3
00:00:08.982 --> 00:00:11.600
because offboarding has no audit signal.

4
00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:14.255
Its deployment guide asks
for a rollback plan,

5
00:00:14.255 --> 00:00:17.538
and its operations guide for
at least two people per role.

6
00:00:17.538 --> 00:00:22.976
The guide adds the rings, the metrics and
the rollback order, with signaling last.

7
00:00:22.976 --> 00:00:26.154
And CISA's remote user
use case says visibility

8
00:00:26.154 --> 00:00:29.175
must be preserved through
telemetry sharing.

9
00:00:29.175 --> 00:00:33.847
One thing isn't rebuilt: the Zero Trust
Assessment results kit already turns an

10
00:00:33.847 --> 00:00:38.663
assessment into the closure register, and
its network family points at the guide.

11
00:00:38.663 --> 00:00:41.810
This chapter's evidence is
what that register cites.
